This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - **(Completed)** Render the rubric's "Full Review (narrative)" as markdown in both the side-panel (`rubric-panel.tsx`) and the full-page report (`routes/rubric/index.tsx`), matching the existing markdown rendering already used in the personas "Full Analysis" feature.
   - **(Completed)** Build a dedicated full-page route for "The Full Analysis" (the persona-room `RoomAnalysis` feature), styled and structured similarly to the existing `/rubric/` page — not just a modal.
   - **(Completed)** Fix a bug in `src/routes/library/index.tsx`: clicking a folio card, or the empty-state "Start writing →" link, navigated to `/` instead of `/editor/`, which only redirects to the editor if a saved project brief exists — meaning users with folios but no brief got stuck on the landing page instead of opening the editor.
   - **(Explained, not a code bug)** User reported `/analysis/` shows "No writer by that handle" in what sounds like production — diagnosed as the new route simply not being deployed yet (verified locally via curl that the dev server correctly serves the real page). Also proactively fixed a related hygiene gap: added `"analysis"` to `RESERVED_HANDLES` in `convex/profiles.ts` so no writer can claim that handle and shadow the route.
   - **(Open, unanswered)** I asked whether to commit and push all pending work to `main` to trigger a production deploy — the user has not yet responded to this question; nothing has been committed or pushed.
   - **(Discussion → now implementing)** User asked "is it possible to get an F?" (answered: yes, mechanically) then "it seems a bit hard to get an F and some of my work i think deserves an F" (diagnosed: the 30%-weighted static/mechanical score props up bad content) then "is thhere another metric that we could add that is weighthed a bit strongly that would make sense" (I proposed a weighted "worst judge" / minimum-judge-score component) then explicitly confirmed: **"okay let's do the min judge"** — this authorized implementing the min-judge blending change.
   - **(New, most recent, in progress)** User said: **"update the card explaining the grades"** — this is the newest instruction, arriving mid-implementation of the min-judge change, and refers to the grade-explainer UI (almost certainly the "Why a 'good' draft is still a C" / brutal-curve explainer card in `src/routes/rubric/index.tsx`, possibly also the grade/color legend) which needs its copy updated to reflect the new weighting scheme (judge mean 45% + worst judge 35% + static features 20%, versus the old 70%/30% judge/static split).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Qwik framework: `component

, `useStore`, `useSignal`, `useVisibleTask

, `useStylesScoped

, `$()` QRLs, `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, Qwik City `Link`, `useNavigate`, `RequestHandler`, file-based routing (`src/routes/<segment>/index.tsx` → `/segment/`).
   - Qwik City dynamic routes: `src/routes/[handle]/index.tsx` is a catch-all single-segment route; static folder routes (like `/analysis/`, `/rubric/`) are expected to take precedence over it once deployed, confirmed via local curl test that this works correctly in dev.
   - Convex: `mutation`/`query`/`action`, args validators (`v.number()`, etc.), `consumeRateLimit` helper, schema tables/indexes.
   - Rubric scoring pipeline (`src/utils/rubric.ts`): `scoreStaticFeatures` → `StaticScore` (mechanical features: length, structure, pacing, evidence, vocabulary, paragraphShape, integrity), judges (`JudgeResult[]`, five personas each scoring 0-10), `combineJudgesAndStatic()` blends judge mean + static total into a 0-10 `combinedTen`, `brutalCurve()` maps 0-100 raw → curved final (compresses 60-80 band, stretches 90+, ≤50 unchanged), `letterGrade()` maps final score to letter (F below 40).
