# Twyne Dossier Architecture Report — brief/dossier singleton vs. per-folio

## 1. Everywhere `ProjectBrief`/"brief"/"dossier" is read or written

### Server (Convex)

**`convex/schema.ts:6-10`** — the table itself, one row per user, no folio key:
```ts
briefs: defineTable({
  userId: v.string(),
  brief: v.any(),
  updatedAt: v.number(),
}).index("by_userId", ["userId"]),
```
Compare `folioContent` (`convex/schema.ts:20-26`), which already carries a `folioId` field and a `by_userId_folioId` compound index — this is the pattern to imitate.

**`convex/sync.ts:36-64`** — `getBrief`/`putBrief`: single-row query/mutation, `.withIndex("by_userId", ...).first()`, no folio arg at all.

**`convex/sync.ts:330-357`** (`pushAll`) — `args.brief` is a single optional `v.any()`, patches/inserts the one `briefs` row by `userId` only (lines ~554-577 in the raw file, single existing-row lookup).

**`convex/sync.ts:489-511` (`pullAll`)** returns `brief: brief?.brief ?? null` / `briefUpdatedAt` as flat top-level fields, mirroring the singleton-per-user model — contrast with `folioContent: folioContent.map((fc) => ({folioId, html, updatedAt}))` in the same return object, which is already an array keyed by folio.

**`mergeFromRemote`-equivalent on the server side** — n/a (merge happens client-side, see §1 client section below).

Also note: `personaNotes`/`personaReplies` rows carry a denormalized `briefTitle: v.optional(v.string())` (`convex/schema.ts:62`, and `convex/sync.ts` `putPersonaNote` args) — a spot-check of anywhere the singleton brief's title leaks into other tables that would need a folio-scoped equivalent if briefs become per-folio.

### Client — storage layer

**`src/utils/lix.ts:19`** — `export const BRIEF_PATH = "/brief.json";` — a single fixed path in one process-wide Lix instance (`getLix()` opens exactly one Lix blob per tab, `src/utils/lix.ts:29-51`). This is the actual live storage mechanism for the brief.

**`src/utils/anti-tabula-rasa.ts:37-65`** — `loadProjectBrief()` / `saveProjectBrief()`:
```ts
export function loadProjectBrief(): ProjectBrief | null {
  ...
  const raw = localStorage.getItem(BRIEF_STORAGE_KEY); // "twyne-project-brief"
  ...
}
export function saveProjectBrief(brief: ProjectBrief): void {
  localStorage.setItem(BRIEF_STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(brief));
  void writeFileAsJson(BRIEF_PATH, brief).then(() => markSyncDirty());
}
```
Double-backed by both `localStorage` (single fixed key `"twyne-project-brief"`) and Lix (`BRIEF_PATH`), both **global, unkeyed by folio**.

**Dead/unused precedent already in idb.ts**: `src/utils/idb.ts:6-8, 44-48, 76-77, 319-353` defines a `brief` object store with `keyPath: "folioId"` and exports `loadBriefFromIdb(folioId)` / `saveBriefToIdb(folioId, brief)` — **but these two functions have zero callers anywhere in `src/`** (confirmed via grep). This looks like a half-finished migration toward per-folio briefs that was abandoned in favor of the global Lix/localStorage path. Worth knowing before designing the real migration.

### Client — sync orchestration (`src/utils/convex-sync.ts`)

**Build snapshot, line 283-284:**
```ts
async function buildLocalSnapshot(): Promise<LocalSnapshot> {
  const brief = (await readFileAsJson<ProjectBrief>(BRIEF_PATH)) ?? null;
  const folios = await loadFoliosFromIdb();
  const activeFolioId = await loadActiveFolioIdFromIdb();
  const ids = new Set<string>(folios.map((f) => f.id));
  if (activeFolioId) ids.add(activeFolioId);
  const folioContent: Array<{ folioId: string; html: string }> = [];
  for (const id of ids) {
    const html = await loadFolioContentFromIdb(id);
    folioContent.push({ folioId: id, html });
  }
  ...
```
One global `brief` read vs. a per-folio loop for `folioContent` — this is the clearest single artifact showing the asymmetry to fix.

**Push, line 330-357 (`pushLocalSnapshot`)** — `brief: snap.brief` sent as one flat field to `api.sync.pushAll`.

**Pull/merge, line 448-459 (`mergeFromRemote`)**:
```ts
if (remote.brief && (local.brief === null || remote.briefUpdatedAt > (local.brief.updatedAt ?? 0))) {
  await writeFileAsJson(BRIEF_PATH, remote.brief);
}
...
// Folio content — per-folio, newer-wins.
for (const fc of remote.folioContent) { ... }
```
Brief: single newer-wins compare. FolioContent: loop over per-folio entries — again the precedent pattern.

**`handleUserChanged` (~line 390-446)** — `hasRemoteData` check at line 422-429 includes `remote.brief !== null` as one of several OR'd conditions gating whether to merge vs. push-to-seed; nothing folio-specific here.

### Client — onboarding / interview flow

**`src/routes/onboarding/index.tsx:69`** — gate check: `if (loadProjectBrief()) { void nav("/editor/"); return; }` — onboarding is entirely independent of folios; it only checks "does *a* brief exist globally," never which folio.

**`src/routes/dossier/create/index.tsx:61-62`**:
```ts
const brief = createProjectBrief(answers, null, attachments);
saveProjectBrief(brief);
```
`previous` is hardcoded `null` — always creates a brand-new global brief, no `folioId` parameter exists anywhere in this route. Not tied to folio creation at all: no `Folio` object is created here.

**`src/routes/dossier/refine/index.tsx:62-76`** — loads/saves the same global singleton (`store.brief = loadProjectBrief()`, `saveProjectBrief(next)`), also loads `draftText` via `loadDraftHtml()` (global localStorage draft key, not per-folio) rather than the active folio's content.

**`src/components/folio/folio-menu.tsx`** — receives `brief: ProjectBrief | null` as a **prop** passed down from the editor route's global `store.brief`, entirely decoupled from `activeFolioId` (also a separate prop). Used e.g. for export metadata (`brief: props.brief` at line 203, 385) and `briefSummary: props.brief?.answers.goal` (line 290) regardless of which folio is active.

### Client — editor (`src/routes/editor/index.tsx`)

**Hydration, lines 175-212** — loads brief exactly once at mount:
```ts
const brief = loadProjectBrief();
const folios = await loadFoliosFromIdb();
const activeFolioId = await loadActiveFolioIdFromIdb();
...
store.brief = brief;
store.hydrated = true;
```

**Folio switch handlers never touch `store.brief`:**
- Switch to existing folio, line 553-566 (`onClick$` on folio list button) — sets `store.activeFolioId`, `store.editorSeed`, dispatches `twyne:load-folio`, but `store.brief` is untouched.
- Create new folio via Enter key, lines 595-620, and via "Create" button, lines 624-646 — same: sets `activeFolioId`/`editorSeed`, never sets/reloads `brief`.
- Sign-out / reset, line 763-765: `store.brief = null; ... store.activeFolioId = null;` — both cleared together only on full local-data nuke, not on ordinary folio switching.

**Background research kickoff, lines 362-383** — `startBackgroundResearch({ client, brief: store.brief, folioId: store.activeFolioId })` is called exactly once inside the top-level `useVisibleTask$` (confirmed only call site via grep — `src/utils/background-research.ts:134` declares it, `src/routes/editor/index.tsx:366` is the only caller). Internally (`src/utils/background-research.ts:136-141`) it stashes `brief`/`folioId` into module-level mutable variables `activeBrief`/`activeFolioId` that are **never refreshed** when the user switches folios in the UI — so background research keeps using the folioId captured at mount even after the writer switches folios.

**Brief passed into AI/UI surfaces**, all reading the single `store.brief`:
- `ProjectBriefCard` — line 527-528 `brief={store.brief}` (renders "The Dossier" card; `src/components/brief/project-brief-card.tsx:4-11`, no folio awareness in the component itself).
- `PersonasPanel` — line 1032 `<PersonasPanel brief={store.brief} />` (`src/components/personas/personas-panel.tsx:130,208` — accepts `brief: ProjectBrief | null` prop, threads it into every persona/agent call, e.g. lines 516, 561, 683, 708, 718, 935, 988, 1165, 1201, and into `summarizeBrief(brief)` at line 1345).
- `RubricPanel` — line 1039 `<RubricPanel brief={store.brief} />` (`src/components/rubric/rubric-panel.tsx:64,67` — same pattern, threads `brief` into judge calls at lines 119, 153, 181, 208, 241, 249, 264, 272, 284, 289, 321, 342, 353).
- Line 1047-1048: another consumer receiving both `brief={store.brief}` and `activeFolioId={store.activeFolioId}` as separate sibling props (comments/apparatus panel) — again the pattern of passing folio id and brief independently, never combined/keyed.

### Client — Convex actions (`convex/agents.ts`)

Every agent action (interview synthesis, persona reply, dossier check, room-of-editors calls) takes `brief` as a raw arg validated by a shared `briefValidator` (line 357) and typed `Partial<ProjectInterviewAnswers>`/`ProjectBrief` — **no `folioId` argument exists in any of these actions** (`convex/agents.ts:525,585,621,699,732,769,795,820,835,895,907` etc. all take `brief` alone, no folio key). This means the AI-facing surface would need a `folioId` threaded through if briefs become per-folio (currently they receive whatever `store.brief` the client passed, unaware of folio at all).

### Other lesser call sites (grep hits, not deeply explored — flagged for completeness)
`src/utils/standard-site.ts`, `src/utils/exchange.ts`, `src/utils/ai-client.ts`, `src/components/comments/comments-panel.tsx`, `src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx`, `src/routes/apparatus/index.tsx`, `src/routes/index.tsx`, `src/routes/auth/callback/index.tsx`, `src/routes/signin/index.tsx` — all reference `ProjectBrief`/brief-passing in the same "global singleton prop" style; none reference a folio id in conjunction with brief.

---

## 2. `Folio` type shape (`src/types/index.ts:254-266`)

```ts
export interface Folio {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  type: "draft" | "notes" | "outline";
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
  layout?: LayoutSettings;
  header?: string;
  footer?: string;
}
```
No `briefId`, no embedded brief data, no goal/audience field of any kind. `ProjectBrief` (`src/types/index.ts:247-252`) is a fully separate interface (`answers: ProjectInterviewAnswers; attachments: DossierAttachment[]; completedAt; updatedAt`) with zero structural link to `Folio`. The two are connected today only by convention/timing (onboarding creates a brief once, then a `Folio` is separately synthesized from legacy draft migration — see editor hydration lines 185-198) — never by an id reference.

---

## 3. Places assuming "the brief" is a singleton

- `src/routes/editor/index.tsx` `LayoutStore.brief: ProjectBrief | null` (line 74) — one field for the whole app, not `Record<folioId, ProjectBrief>` or similar.
- `src/utils/anti-tabula-rasa.ts` — `loadProjectBrief()`/`saveProjectBrief()` have no folio parameter; `BRIEF_STORAGE_KEY` is one fixed localStorage key.
- `src/utils/lix.ts` — `BRIEF_PATH = "/brief.json"` fixed path, one Lix instance per tab (module-level `_lix`/`_lixPromise` singletons, `src/utils/lix.ts:23-25`).
- `convex/schema.ts` `briefs` table — one row per `userId`, index `by_userId` only (no `by_userId_folioId` twin, unlike `folioContent`).
- `src/utils/background-research.ts` — module-level `activeBrief`/`activeFolioId` mutable singletons (lines 136-141), set once.
- `src/components/rubric/rubric-panel.tsx` and `src/components/personas/personas-panel.tsx` — both take `brief: ProjectBrief | null` as a single prop, no `folioId` correlation inside the component (folioId is a wholly separate, uncombined prop on sibling components).
- `dossier/create` and `dossier/refine` routes — no `folioId` in scope at all, operate purely on the global brief.

The one **already-correct** precedent for what per-folio storage/sync should look like is `folioContent`: `src/utils/idb.ts` (`folio-content` object store, `keyPath: "folioId"`), `convex/schema.ts:20-26` (`folioContent` table + `by_userId_folioId` index), `convex/sync.ts` `pushAll`/`pullAll` looping per-folio-id, and `src/utils/convex-sync.ts:290-295` looping `for (const id of ids)`.

---

## 4. `activeFolioId` mechanics (multi-folio switching)

**Storage**: `src/utils/idb.ts:357-369` — `loadActiveFolioIdFromIdb()` reads a single `meta` record keyed `"active-folio-id"` (`MetaRecord { key, value, updatedAt }`, singleton — same "meta" store pattern used for other single-value settings). Corresponding `saveActiveFolioIdToIdb` (used at `src/routes/editor/index.tsx:198, 560, 614, 644` — grep confirms these are the only writers).

**Read on hydration**: `src/routes/editor/index.tsx:177` — `const activeFolioId = await loadActiveFolioIdFromIdb();` then `store.activeFolioId = activeFolioId ?? folios[0].id;` (line 206) as part of the same `useVisibleTask$` that loads `brief` (line 175) — currently these two loads are siblings in the same block but never re-correlated afterward.

**Set on user folio switch**: `src/routes/editor/index.tsx:556` (switch to existing folio — also updates `editorSeed` via `loadFolioContentFromIdb(folio.id)` at line 555, i.e. per-folio content swap already happens here) and lines 607/637 (new-folio creation) — all three call `void saveActiveFolioIdToIdb(...)` to persist the new active id, and dispatch/set `editorSeed`, but **none set/reload `store.brief`**.

**Sync layer's own read of active folio**: `src/utils/convex-sync.ts:286-288` uses `loadActiveFolioIdFromIdb()` only to make sure the active folio's content id is included in the `folioContent` set being pushed (`ids.add(activeFolioId)`), not for anything brief-related.

**Net finding for the design task**: the plumbing to swap per-folio state already exists and is exercised for `editorSeed`/`folioContent` on every folio switch (`loadFolioContentFromIdb(folio.id)` → `store.editorSeed`) — the brief simply isn't wired into that same switch path anywhere, and both the client storage (`localStorage` + Lix `BRIEF_PATH`) and server table (`briefs` by `userId` only) would need a `folioId` dimension added, mirroring `folioContent`'s `by_userId_folioId` index, to make the brief swap alongside content when `store.activeFolioId` changes.

